{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DUPLICATE of epic e594-e1d0-74f4-4d40 (bronze-used-foxhound), 'Bound tickets-repo growth: shrink reconciler .bridge_state on-branch', which is TABLED at status=idea and already contains a far more thorough analysis — including the same root cause (baseline_advanced_at as a write-only timestamp bumped unconditionally every pass), four history dossiers on why the current design exists, and a sequenced 4-step plan.\n\nClosing in favour of e594. The fresh measurements from this ticket have been posted as a comment there: the problem has more than doubled since e594 was tabled (bridge_state 375 MB -> 942.5 MB; bindings.json 987 -> 3,009 versions), and aggressive repack has been ruled out as a lever (8,157 of 8,165 bridge-state blobs are already deltified at avg depth 13.9)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785350239662657001,"uuid":"9dae72ad-a08b-4f12-acef-f6f831c6d008"}